  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not lock in NDA, CDS, TES, or Agnipath purely from the "prestige" version of the story you have
    heard from one relative or one recruitment reel.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Run yourself through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above, honestly, on paper — with your family in the
      room if the decision affects them, which it will.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then match the entry route to your actual stage: NDA or TES if you are certain at 12th, CDS if you
      want a degree first, and Agnipath if you want the lowest-commitment way to genuinely test the fit
      before deciding on a longer officer track.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Achieving earlier financial freedom and a stable long-term career through defence service depends on
    matching the entry route and commission type to your real tolerance for postings, hierarchy, and family
    disruption — not just picking whichever exam sounds most respected. Move toward that decision with
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    if you want a second opinion on your specific situation, or start with the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a>
    if you are still unsure whether structured, hierarchy-heavy work genuinely fits your working style.
  </p>

